This landmark documentary provides a vibrant snapshot of the 1980s through the eyes of
New York City's African American and Latinx Harlem drag-ball scene.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Made over seven years, PARIS IS BURNING offers an intimate portrait of rival fashion "houses," from fierce contests for trophies
to house mothers offering sustenance in a world rampant with homophobia, transphobia, racism, AIDS, and poverty.

